

🧩 Creating a DFDL Schema File (IBM IIB)

🔹 Purpose:

DFDL schema file is used to model text and binary formatted data (like CSV, COBOL, or C data) for integration message parsing.


---

🧠 DFDL can model these formats:

Format Type	Description

CSV (Comma Separated Value)	For delimited data with separators like , or `
Record-Oriented Text	For line-by-line or fixed record files
Custom Text/Binary	For proprietary or legacy formats
COBOL Data Structures	You can import COBOL copybooks and auto-generate schema
C Data Structures	You can import from C header files (.h) to generate schema (some restrictions apply)



---

⚙️ Creating via New Message Model Wizard:

Steps:

1. Open New Message Model Wizard:

From Navigator → New → Message Model..., or

Right-click the navigator white space → New → Message Model...



2. Choose Data Format Type:
Select whether you’re modeling CSV, Record-Oriented, COBOL, C, or Custom Binary/Text.


3. Step through the wizard panels:
Fill in details (name, location, format options).


4. Click Finish:
DFDL schema file (.xsd) is created.


5. Open automatically in DFDL Schema Editor to view/edit/test it.




---

🔜 Next Steps:

Edit properties in DFDL editor.

Configure object-level settings.

Test schema with sample input data.



